#!/bin/sh
# xwayland-sw - Xwayland for a session the CPU draws (sway with pixman:
# safe mode, and virtual machines without 3D). session-run points
# wlroots at it (WLR_XWAYLAND) there and nowhere else.
#
# Started as wlroots starts it, Xwayland sets up glamor - its GL - on the
# render node, and under LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE, which the same session
# sets, Mesa crashes in that setup (driCreateNewScreen3, "Not allowed to
# force software rendering when API explicitly selects a hardware
# device"). Xwayland died before its first client, the X11 socket was
# never there, and no X11 program could open a window at all - Steam
# among them, whose client is X11 only. XWAYLAND_NO_GLAMOR is read after
# that setup, too late; -shm keeps Xwayland off GL from the start, which
# is how everything else in this session draws anyway.
exec /usr/bin/Xwayland "$@" -shm
